## Step 1: Identify the Big Problem
### Main Problem
The school canteen is inefficient during lunch break. Because of this, it causes overcrowding and long lines for students.
---
## Step 2: Identify the Sub-Problems
1. Students spend too much time at the counter deciding their order.
2. The cashier has to process cash and change by hand.
3. The canteen may experience unexpected food shortages due to having no system to track stock levels.
4. The canteen may be small and could lack in organized lines to handle the amount of students during lunch time.
---
## Step 3: Apply Computational Thinking Skills
| Sub-Problem | CT Skill | Proposed Solution |
|---|---|---|
| Sub-problem 1 | Abstraction | Create a digital menu so that students will know what to order beforehand. |
| Sub-problem 2 | Algorithms | Create a system that accepts digital payments, which will help in calculating totals and eliminating handling cash manually. |
| Sub-problem 3 | Pattern Recognition | Analyze sales logs from previous weeks to predict what items are in demand to prepare in advance. |
| Sub-problem 4 | Decomposition | Divide the canteen into multiple zones. One for ordering food and another zone for claiming orders.|
---
## Step 4: Algorithmic Solution
### Selected Sub-Problem
Sub-problem 4
### Pseudocode
START
Student enters Canteen
	
		Proceed to OrderingQueue
IF Counter is free THEN
		Place Order
		Process Payment
		Generated OrderTicket
ENDIF
Exit OrderingQueue

Move to ClaimingQueue

IF OrderTicket is claimed
		Receive Order
ENDIF
	
	Exit Canteen
END
